title: 'P8-D97 round 2: kernel memory audit, shell preprocessing fails closed, production-policy probe'
summary: 'Aegis H1-H3, M1-M3, Q6 and reviewer 1/2/4/5 built. Probe p10m-repo-context round 2 under the PRODUCTION policy (no allow rules) passed 12 checks. Denial sources: a read of another session''s file, direct or through a shell variable, was denied by a policy.json deny rule with no can_use_tool request (Claude resolves the variable); osascript was allowed on its card and then refused by the sandbox (exit 126); no classifier was involved. Without the setting, a skill''s inline ! shell hits the always-ask Bash rule and fails closed with no request; with disableSkillShellExecution in --settings, both the Skill tool and a user-typed /project:zsh get a placeholder. The first rerun was refused by the model as exfiltration-shaped, so the steps are now separate turns. A scratch HOME needs CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN from claude setup-token (not available here), so the founder ~/.claude user-layer confound is recorded in the result.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#supervisor'
  - '#claude-adapter'
  - '#manifest-loader'
tags:
  - gnomon
  - p8-d97
  - probe
  - aegis
learnings:
  - split probe turns so one model refusal cannot mask the other measurements
  - disableSkillShellExecution is honoured from the kernel --settings file
  - Claude resolves shell variables when matching Bash commands against deny rules
